WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s been a very strange year
in football because I think

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of people like you
who love the game

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
and want to cover the game...
-Yeah.

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:08.375
-...all of a sudden, politics
has been a huge part of the NFL

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:11.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
this year, many have said
to its detriment.

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.980
Has it been frustrating being
in a position where you want

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
to talk about the sports
of it to also

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
have to balance it with...
-Sure.

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:20.153 size:88% position:44%
Yeah, ´cause you know,
I have a Twitter account

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:23.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
where anytime something
like this comes up,

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
I get the "Stick to sports,
stick to football,

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.728
stick to something other
than the fact that you have

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
a mind of your own to
actually speak on something."

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:37.003
Which is what I view these
players who are taking a knee

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:39.072 size:75% position:38%
before a game during
the National Anthem,

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:43.276
That they are having a moment
to try and bring attention

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:48.548
to an American experience that
maybe not everybody is aware of.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:53.720 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:58.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
And yet, at the same time --
at the same time,

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:02.262
it´s fine that when I go to
a game and my kids are there,

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:04.431
I make them stand and put
their hand over their heart

00:01:04.431 --> 00:01:08.268
and take their hat off and stand
for the National Anthem.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:11.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just in the same way.
that´s what I want to do,

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:15.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
the players are doing this
not to be combative

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:17.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
towards first responders
or the military,

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:21.481
but rather to call attention
to something that they want

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have changed.

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:28.555 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I have met members
of the military who say,

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:31.958 size:81% position:41%
"That´s why I fought."

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ve met members of
the military who are offended.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:38.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ve met people who are fine
on either side.

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:42.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
And just having a conversation
is what I think this is

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
the most important thing.
-Do you think that --

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I´ve watched
a lot of panels,

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:50.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
with people like yourself,
ex-coaches, ex-athletes

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:53.513
having conversations about this,
conversations that I had not

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
seen before on
these kind of shows.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:57.550
Do you think those conversations
are getting through at all

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:01.121
to people, or do you think
people are so angry at one side

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.856
or the other there´s no sort
of amount of conversation?

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:05.258
-I think it´s both.
And it think it´s -- It´s both.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:08.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think there are some people
who are hearing this

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:11.731
and understanding that
there is a larger picture

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:14.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the players are trying
to draw attention to.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then there are others
who just are saying

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.938
they´re turning the sets off.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.374
And to me, they´re missing
some really great football.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:22.909
-Yeah.
-Quite honestly, but, you know.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:27.347
That´s -- That´s something
tat I´ve seen for years,

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:30.250
is that there´s always going
to be something from outside

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.352
the football world that takes...
-Finds its way in.

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:33.853
-Right, that finds its way in.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.789
In this case, having a national
conversation about it I think,

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:37.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
is fine.

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
